==German==

===Etymology===
From {{der|de|gmh|gegen}}, from {{der|de|goh|gagan}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*gagin}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|tegen}}, {{cog|en|against}}, {{cog|is|gegn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɡe.ɡən/|[ˈɡeː.ɡn̩]|[ˈɡeː.ɡŋ̍]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-gegen.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Preposition===
{{head|de|preposition}} {{lb|de|+ accusative}}

# [[against]]
#: {{ux|de|[[der|Der]] [[Erklärung]] der [[Vereinten Nationen]] [[über]] [[die]] [[Beseitigung]] der [[Gewalt]] '''gegen''' [[Frauen]].|translation=[[the|The]] [[United Nations]] [[declaration|Declaration]] [[on]] the [[elimination|Elimination]] [[of]] [[violence|Violence]] '''against''' [[women|Women]].}}

====Usage notes====
* Like its Middle High German predecessor, ''gegen'' was formerly also used with the dative, especially by [[Upper German]] writers. Compare {{m|de|entgegen}}, which still takes dative.

